1
00:05:42,222 --> 00:05:48,222
It's about life. It's about love. It's about us.

2
00:11:24,444 --> 00:11:30,444
The Color Purple is a drama, history film directed by Steven Spielberg.

3
00:17:06,666 --> 00:17:12,666
An epic tale spanning forty years in the life of Celie, an African-American woman
living in the South who survives incredible abuse and bigotry.

4
00:22:48,888 --> 00:22:54,888
After Celie's abusive father marries her off to the equally debasing 'Mister' Albert Johnson,
things go from bad to worse, leaving Celie to find companionship anywhere she can.

5
00:28:31,111 --> 00:28:37,111
She perseveres, holding on to her dream of one day
being reunited with her sister in Africa.

6
00:34:13,333 --> 00:34:19,333
Albert, played by Danny Glover.

7
00:39:55,555 --> 00:40:01,555
Celie, played by Whoopi Goldberg.

8
00:45:37,777 --> 00:45:43,777
Shug Avery, played by Margaret Avery.

9
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
Sofia, played by Oprah Winfrey.

10
00:57:02,222 --> 00:57:08,222
Harpo, played by Willard E. Pugh.

11
01:02:44,444 --> 01:02:50,444
Nettie, played by Akosua Busia.

12
01:08:26,666 --> 01:08:32,666
The Color Purple is a 1985 American epic period drama film, directed by Steven Spielberg
and written by Menno Meyjes, based on the 1982 novel by Alice Walker.

13
01:14:08,888 --> 01:14:14,888
Spielberg's eighth film as a director, it marked a turning point in his career as it was
a departure from the summer blockbusters for which he had become known.

14
01:19:51,111 --> 01:19:57,111
It is the first film directed by Spielberg for which John Williams did not
compose the score, which was done by Quincy Jones instead.

15
01:25:33,333 --> 01:25:39,333
Jones also produced the film alongside Spielberg,
Kathleen Kennedy and Frank Marshall.

16
01:31:15,555 --> 01:31:21,555
The film stars Whoopi Goldberg in her breakthrough role, along with Danny Glover,
Oprah Winfrey (in her film debut), Margaret Avery, and Adolph Caesar.

17
01:36:57,777 --> 01:37:03,777
Filmed in Anson and Union counties in North Carolina, The Color Purple tells the coming-of-age story of a young African-American girl named Celie
Harris and the brutal experiences she endured including domestic violence, incest, child sexual abuse, poverty, racism, and sexism.

18
01:42:40,000 --> 01:42:46,000
Upon its release by Warner Bros.

19
01:48:22,222 --> 01:48:28,222
on December 18, 1985, The Color Purple was a box office success,
grossing $98.4 million against a budget of $15 million.

20
01:54:04,444 --> 01:54:10,444
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, with praise going to its acting (especially Goldberg's performance), direction,
screenplay, musical score, and production values; criticism was directed by some for being "over-sentimental" and "stereotypical".

21
01:59:46,666 --> 01:59:52,666
The film was nominated for 11 Academy Awards, including Best
Picture, but did not achieve a single win.

22
02:05:28,888 --> 02:05:34,888
It holds the record for most Oscar nominations without one for Best Director.

23
02:11:11,111 --> 02:11:17,111
It also received four Golden Globe Award nominations, with
Goldberg winning Best Actress in a Drama.

24
02:16:53,333 --> 02:16:59,333
In 2006, the American Film Institute ranked the film 51st
on its list of the most inspiring movies.

25
02:22:35,555 --> 02:22:41,555
The film explores themes of prison, rape, sibling
relationship, jazz, southern usa.

26
02:28:17,777 --> 02:28:23,777
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and emotional.
